US-002 is implemented. Here's a summary of what was done:

**Files changed:**
- `src/login.html` — Added localStorage check on load (auto-redirect to dashboard if valid token exists); stores `popo_token` in localStorage after successful login
- `src/dashboard.html` — Added logout button; persists token to localStorage on render; `doLogout()` calls `serverLogout()` + `getLoginHtml()` and clears localStorage
- `src/auth.gs` — Added `serverLogout(token)` (removes cache entry) and `getLoginHtml()` (returns login page HTML for client-side replacement)
- `tests/auth.spec.ts` — Created with US-002 describe block: 4 tests covering login page visibility, wrong password error message, correct login → dashboard heading, and logout → back to login with localStorage cleared

**Key design decision:** GAS `doGet` runs server-side before client JS, so the token can't be read from localStorage at the server. Instead, `doGet` always serves the login shell; client-side JS handles the token check and auto-navigation. All page transitions use `document.write(html)` with the token carried through JS variables.

